<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Balkan War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1913</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Balkan War was fought from June to August 1913 after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, dissatisfied with the division of Ottoman lands won in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-balkan-war">First Balkan War</a>, attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> then joined against Bulgaria, which was quickly defeated. By the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bucharest">Bucharest</a> Bulgaria lost most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-region">Macedonia</a>, and Romania gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-dobruja">Southern Dobruja</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-balkan-war.jpg" alt="Second Balkan War" width="320" height="257" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kandi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Second_Balkan_War.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
